// content/maps/earth/resources.ron — Earth resource layer: tags per land region (WS-08b §4.4, WLD-076). DRAFT, pending OQ-S1.
// Geology is physical geography: setting-agnostic, no polity IDs (ARC-052). Offshore fields attach to the coastal land
// region because sea zones are never owned (WLD-010). Tag grammar: <kind>.<size class>[.<qualifier>]*, kind without "res.".
// Knowledge at 1955-01 [R, from the real discovery history]: default known; "suspected" = basin known, size not;
// "unknown" = found after 1955 in our world (e.g. West Siberia 1960s, North Sea 1969, Prudhoe Bay 1968).
// One deposit is generated per tag; its truth is drawn per world, so a tag sets the odds, not the outcome.
[
    ("region.arabia_gulf",        ["hydrocarbons.supergiant.easy", "hydrocarbons.giant.offshore"]),
    ("region.khuzestan",          ["hydrocarbons.giant.easy"]),
